Here is data coming from a balloon, as high as the Eiffel all, and whose utility is to test new technology applications before being placed on satellites for long-duration space missions.

This dataset contains the telemetry data obtained from the different sub systems during the AUSTRAL2017 mission and two sets of pictures from different cameras. The Canadian Space Agency (CSA) STRATOS program participated in the AUSTRAL2017 flight campaign which took place in Australia on April 8, 2017. One of the goals of this flight was to launch hardware at altitudes of around 40 kilometres and observe the different data that was captured throughout the flight. The available data concern:
1 - Raw A2D data from battery fail safe card;
2 - Housekeeping data from battery fail safe card;
3 - A2D from battery fail safe card, converted to engineering unit;
4 - Data Acquisition Module (Rasp.Pi) - Hardware related telemetry;
